# A row that is no list was asked for a Float64Array alone; rows that are Float32Arrays ran the stretch as written, five accesses by stubs. Behind the Float64Array the row is asked for each kind of view that is
# seen to arrive at the read, and each kind has an arm of its own: the row's length is read once in it.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=Float64Array
# CHECK: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=Float32Array
# CHECK: = GetTypedArrayLength {{*}} typedArrayType=9
# CHECK: = PutTypedArrayElement {{*}} typedArrayType=9 {{*}}level=Proven
# CHECK: = PutTypedArrayElement {{*}} typedArrayType=9 {{*}}level=Proven
# RUN(COUNT): compile RowsThatAreNoListsAskedForViews mechanisms=all
